# Runtime config is COMMITTED on purpose — see the header of config.js.
# A static site cannot read environment variables, and config.js holds only
# the public Supabase URL and the publishable (anon) key, which is safe to
# expose: RLS is what protects the data. Never add a service_role key or any
# private token to it. config.example.js stays as the template for a clone.

# Agent / editor scratch space: timestamped copies of files taken before edits.
.freebuff/

# Local logs (dev server output, preview logs).
*.log
server.log

# Dependencies (this project has none, but never commit a stray install).
node_modules/

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
